    inGuideTitle: 'Inbound Management Guide',
    inGuideIntro: 'This guide explains all inbound-related processes step by step. Easy to follow for new staff.',
    inGuide1Title: '1. What is Inbound Management?',
    inGuide1_1: 'Inbound is the process of registering goods received from vendors into the system.',
    inGuide1_2: 'When you register an inbound, it reflects in stock increase, accounts payable, and income statement purchases.',
    inGuide1_3: 'Whether from a purchase order or direct purchase, stock and purchases are finalized at the inbound registration time.',
    inGuide2Title: '2. Overall Flow',
    inGuide2_1: 'Create PO ? Approve ? Register Inbound ? Stock & Payable updated',
    inGuide2_2: 'Or Direct Purchase ? Register Inbound ? Same reflection',
    inGuide2_3: 'Bank withdrawal ? Link to Inbound to track which inbound was paid',
    inGuide3Title: '3. How to Register New Inbound',
    inGuide3_1: 'Date: Select the actual receipt date.',
    inGuide3_2: 'Vendor: Select the vendor. Add new vendors in Vendor Management first.',
    inGuide3_3: 'Add items: Use ?? to search and select items, enter quantity, then click "Add to List".',
    inGuide3_4: 'Edit cost: Items have default cost; you can edit the table if actual cost differs.',
    inGuide3_5: 'Save: Click "Process Inbound" to save. Stock and payable are updated automatically.',
    inGuide4Title: '4. Inbound from Purchase Order',
    inGuide4_1: 'Approved purchase orders have an "Register Inbound" button.',
    inGuide4_2: 'Click to go to inbound screen with items, qty, and cost pre-filled from the PO.',
    inGuide4_3: 'For partial receipt, edit quantities and save.',
    inGuide5Title: '5. View, Edit, Delete Inbound',
    inGuide5_1: 'Use the History tab to filter by date, vendor, and store.',
    inGuide5_2: 'Edit: Click pencil icon to edit vendor, invoice no. For item/qty changes, delete and re-register is safer.',
    inGuide5_3: 'Delete: Trash icon removes the inbound. Stock and payable are also updated.',
    inGuide6Title: '6. Bank Withdrawal & Inbound Linking',
    inGuide6_1: 'Purchase payment withdrawals have an "Inbound Link" button (??) in the Bank tab.',
    inGuide6_2: 'Click to see inbound batches for that vendor. Enter amounts paid for each inbound.',
    inGuide6_3: 'One withdrawal can be split across multiple inbound batches.',
    inGuide6_4: 'If vendor is not set, select vendor first in the dialog, then link inbounds.',
    inGuide7Title: '7. Stock, P&L, Payable Link',
    inGuide7_1: 'Stock: Inbound is recorded in stock_logs and reflected in stock reports.',
    inGuide7_2: 'Purchases: Income statement uses inbound only. PO approval does not count as purchase.',
    inGuide7_3: 'Payable: Created at inbound registration. Link to bank withdrawal to track settlements.',
    inGuide8Title: '8. Notes',
    inGuide8_1: 'Enter date, vendor, items, qty, and cost accurately for correct P&L and stock.',
    inGuide8_2: 'Fix or delete and re-register quickly if there is an error.',
    inGuide8_3: 'Link bank withdrawals to inbounds carefully for easy settlement tracking.',
